WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.179 --> 00:00:05.790
Five years ago I spent $5000 on trashcan Mac
Pro, it was expensive but was the right move

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.229
for me at the time.

00:00:07.229 --> 00:00:11.650
Fast forward to today when Apple just announced
the next Mac Pro, a machine that so many Mac

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.540
fans have been waiting for, and the overall
consensus is that they missed the mark.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.690
Since the release of the trashcan Mac Pro
my video business has grown at least 4x so

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:23.430
I could definitely afford a new Mac Pro, but
there's no way that I’m going to buy one,

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:24.900
and I’ll explain exactly why.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.520
Before you dislike this video and leave a
nasty comment hear me out until the end and

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.420
I think you’ll end up agreeing with me,
and if you don’t the go ahead and comment

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.689
all you want.

00:00:32.689 --> 00:00:36.300
Apple made a key mistake with the new Mac
Pro, and like many pro’s flooding to the

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:40.430
comments sections of Youtube videos and Mac
websites, now that apple cards have revealed,

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:44.140
I’ve decided not going to buy this stainless
steel and aluminum beauty.

00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:48.510
What is a Professional anyways, well, the
definition comes up as a person “engaged

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:53.550
in a specified activity as one's main paid
occupation, rather than as a pastime.”

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.239
As many Apple apologists are pointing out,
that's who Apple targeting with the Mac Pro.

00:00:58.239 --> 00:01:02.460
Not prosumers, hobbyists, or people who just
want a Mac Pro for the cool factor.

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.500
Real working Pro’s.

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:08.290
And the working pro market, “those who are
engaged in an specific activity as their main

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:12.970
paid occupation” has been absolutely exploding
even since the original Mac pro was released.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:18.500
From about 7 million to in 2006 to an expected
42 million by next year.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.979
A huge number of those working Pro’s as
creatives like web developers, photographers,

00:01:22.979 --> 00:01:27.479
videographers, graphics artists, animators,
and yes, full-time Youtubers.

00:01:27.479 --> 00:01:31.979
What is Apple doing to capture this new market
that's in its prime to invest in a solid computer

00:01:31.979 --> 00:01:33.850
that can be expanded long term?

00:01:33.850 --> 00:01:39.720
Well, charging $6000 for a weak base configuration
that will likely need to be specced up closer

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:43.680
to $8 or $10 thousand dollars to offer decent
performance for the money.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:47.680
Please don’t get me wrong, I am not an Apple
hater, far from it actually.

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:52.340
My family practically lives on expensive Apple
devices, and a lot of these are excellent

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:55.710
and worth the money, but with the new Mac
Pro Apple is still out touch.

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:59.420
In the past, it was with their slow upgrade
cycles and trying to make everything sealed

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:08.030
or proprietary, or just trying to be too “courageous”
or “innovative”, but this time its the

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:09.529
price points.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:12.579
Sure there are still pro’s that will end
up using these, most of which are employees

00:02:12.579 --> 00:02:16.760
for corporations or large production houses
that have huge profits and need the write-offs,

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:21.559
but from what I’ve seen working in this
industry those positions are slowly shrinking

00:02:21.559 --> 00:02:24.569
as many go off to pursue a creative profession
themselves where they can afford a $3 to $5000

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:25.569
Mac like I could 5 years ago but can’t afford
an $8,000 model.

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:29.719
The Mac Pro used to be great for this market
which is now roughly 3-4x larger than before.

00:02:29.719 --> 00:02:34.900
Every previous Mac Pro has started at around
$3000 when adjusted for inflation, a good

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:39.319
entry level price point for a base level pro
computer that can be upgraded when needed

00:02:39.319 --> 00:02:40.719
and when budget allows.

00:02:40.719 --> 00:02:44.761
I think everyone would agree that Apple made
the right move going back to a modular Mac

00:02:44.761 --> 00:02:49.439
Pro, but what is the point if the base system
is out of reach for most of the working pro’s,

00:02:49.439 --> 00:02:51.180
and even then the specs are weak.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:56.199
I don’t mind it starting with 8 core CPU
which is no longer a high core count or impressive

00:02:56.199 --> 00:03:02.739
in terms of performance, a 3 year old graphics
card that launched at $230, or a measly 256GB

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:09.059
of SSD that's slower than a MacBook Pro’sm,
is the same base config that was offered 6

00:03:09.059 --> 00:03:12.819
years ago, being 4x smaller than the iMac
Pro’s.

00:03:12.819 --> 00:03:18.689
Or even 32GB of RAM which is not bad in and
of itself, until you realize that those Xeons

00:03:18.689 --> 00:03:23.751
are designed to be used with 6 channel memory,
and Apple is shipping it with 4...

00:03:23.751 --> 00:03:24.751
All of that could be excusable for the base
model, since the previous base models were

00:03:24.751 --> 00:03:25.751
also typically somewhat slow for the time,
but those Mac Pro’s cost $3000, not $6000.

00:03:25.751 --> 00:03:30.249
I understand the need to offer a $40,000 computer
for large companies, but why not also give

00:03:30.249 --> 00:03:34.870
lower budget working pros the chance to get
in the door like they have with every past

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:35.870
Mac pro.

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:40.099
Well, for a few reasons, first off they are
going back to a modular system which means

00:03:40.099 --> 00:03:44.370
they have less control on how much they can
make since you can upgrade parts yourself,

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:47.859
so they need to have a good profit from the
very beginning.

00:03:47.859 --> 00:03:49.349
Second is the iMac Pro.

00:03:49.349 --> 00:03:54.829
When Apple admitted the trashcan as a failure
in 2017 they promised a modular mac in a few

00:03:54.829 --> 00:04:00.059
years but announced the iMac Pro in the time
being which made it almost seem like a stop

00:04:00.059 --> 00:04:01.059
gap.

00:04:01.059 --> 00:04:05.340
Since Apple priced the Pro at $6000 it seems
like the iMac Pro it's definitely here to

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:09.799
stay long term, and the only way to guarantee
not cannibalizing this high end all in one

00:04:09.799 --> 00:04:13.449
is by pricing the Mac Pro higher with lower
specs.

00:04:13.449 --> 00:04:18.239
Apple profits have been going down recently,
and to combat it they are trying to compensate

00:04:18.239 --> 00:04:20.230
by raising the average sales price of their
products.

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.230
In the past, they would replace parts with
latest and greatest, like making new more

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.230
powerful and efficient graphics like the Vega
16 and 20 standard in new MacBooks, but now

00:04:22.230 --> 00:04:23.230
it's a paid $250 or $350 upgrade and the base
is a GPU that launched 3 years ago.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:25.210
If they can raise the base price they will,
like the new MacMini’s, Macbook Air’s

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.500
and even iPhones.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:30.920
For products that need to stay at an entry-level
price, they keep it outdated, like the base

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:35.319
13” Macbook Pro that still ships with the
faulty 2nd gen butterfly keyboard instead

00:04:35.319 --> 00:04:40.379
of being updated to the 4th revision, and
dual-core processors where the whole industry

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:42.009
has moved to quadcore.

00:04:42.009 --> 00:04:46.970
Apples been saying that the PC market is shrinking
and their trashcan Mac Pro sales were single

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.653
digits of their overall sales, but maybe that's
not because there's no market.

00:04:49.653 --> 00:04:53.560
Maybe that’s because the trashcan couldn’t
be upgraded which forced people to look elsewhere,

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:58.120
and many those that stuck around waiting are
now outpriced from the new Mac Pro.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:02.240
With this price point, Apple is clearly targeting
corporations and high-profit studios, but

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:07.060
that market is much smaller than the millions
of Pro’s and Mac fans that have side hustles

00:05:07.060 --> 00:05:11.400
or just those love and can afford $3000 desktop
Mac.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:15.669
Nope, the Mac Pro is no longer for them, only
for the elites.

00:05:15.669 --> 00:05:20.130
Some will reluctantly end up sealed iMacs
that they’ve been trying to avoid, but judging

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:24.419
by the comments on Apple-centric website and
Youtube channels, for many this will be the

00:05:24.419 --> 00:05:26.300
final straw that will force them away for
Apple.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.300
This isn’t a bad machine, honestly I love
how it looks and what Apple is doing with

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.300
it, but along with many other I would have
preferred a lower cost base price even if

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.300
it meant not having that premium aluminum
and stainless enclosure that probably costs

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.300
a fortune to make, or that 1.4 KW power supply
in even the base model.

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:31.300
I think that would make more sense sales wise,
and as a thank you to the hardcore mac fanbase

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:32.300
that has been holding on for years, but hey,
only time will tell.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:33.300
Thank you for watching this video, if you
agree please give it a thumbs up and leave

00:05:33.300 --> 00:05:34.300
a nice comment to offset the negative ones,
if you want to see more videos like this one

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:38.530
click above to subscribe and go ahead and
check out our video on everything new in the

00:05:38.530 --> 00:05:48.819
iPadOS, which is actually an awesome move
from Apple.

